WEBVTT

00:08.675 --> 00:11.769
<i>Magical Witch Punie- chan</i>

00:11.945 --> 00:14.880
<i>Spin that Princess Rod.</i>

00:15.181 --> 00:18.116
<i>She has descended
from the land of magic.</i>

00:18.451 --> 00:21.579
<i>Spin that magical stick.</i>

00:21.688 --> 00:24.680
<i>Pleased to meet you, Punie Tanaka.</i>

00:24.891 --> 00:31.353
<i>Lightning, sweep, exterminate,
use your powers and rule the world.</i>

00:31.498 --> 00:36.299
<i>Don't trust those kind
words and nice smiles.</i>

00:39.706 --> 00:45.474
<i>Lyrical Tokarev, kill them all.</i>

00:45.779 --> 00:52.412
<i>I will take you to the land of paradise.</i>

00:52.685 --> 00:58.749
<i>Lyrical Tokarev, kill them all.</i>

00:58.858 --> 01:07.664
<i>There's only one way
to survive, and that is to fight.</i>

01:15.241 --> 01:26.277
<i>There's only one path that leads
to supremacy, and that is by fighting.</i>

01:31.424 --> 01:34.825
We have midterms
starting today. How depressing.

01:34.928 --> 01:38.022
I envy you, Tetsuko.
You're an honors student.

01:38.131 --> 01:39.894
That's not true.

01:40.533 --> 01:42.933
Oh, I can't wait for the exams.

01:43.303 --> 01:46.204
Shall I show you
how much I've studied?

01:46.306 --> 01:50.436
What? You'll show it to
us here, paya? What a waste, paya.

01:51.010 --> 01:52.136
Studied?

01:52.245 --> 01:53.974
Here we go!

01:55.782 --> 01:56.416
2x2. 2x3. 2x4.

01:56.416 --> 01:59.180
2x2. 2x3. 2x4.
4. 6. 8.

01:59.285 --> 01:59.886
2x5. 2x6. 2x7. 2x8.

01:59.886 --> 02:03.617
2x5. 2x6. 2x7. 2x8.
10. 12. 14. 16.

02:03.723 --> 02:04.357
2x9.

02:04.357 --> 02:05.688
2x9.
1...

02:09.095 --> 02:09.896
18!

02:09.896 --> 02:11.124
18!
You're amazing!

02:11.231 --> 02:13.461
You mastered this section, paya!

02:13.566 --> 02:16.433
That's like elementary-school level.

02:17.170 --> 02:19.604
They can't go up to sixth level...

02:19.706 --> 02:24.370
That's equivalent to the land of
magic's old-emperor level, paya!

02:24.477 --> 02:26.308
You must be...

02:26.713 --> 02:27.737
...stupid.

02:28.014 --> 02:28.548
No! Don't say that!

02:28.548 --> 02:30.650
<i>Stupid
No! Don't say that!</i>

02:30.650 --> 02:33.619
<i>Episode 5: Can You Decide
Someone's Value with Test Scores?</i>

02:33.720 --> 02:36.120
<i>'m Probably a Zero Anyway.
That's Right.</i>

02:36.456 --> 02:41.519
This is hilarious. The princess
from the land of magic is an idiot.

02:49.102 --> 02:51.730
Will you be okay, Punie-chan?

02:51.838 --> 02:55.274
If you do poorly on these
midterms, you'll repeat the grade.

02:55.375 --> 02:58.105
Don't worry. I've taken care of it.

03:06.553 --> 03:07.577
Ouch!

03:09.022 --> 03:11.149
Class is already in session.

03:11.658 --> 03:14.650
Quiet. Put away everything
but your writing implements.

03:14.761 --> 03:18.288
G-Gesomi!
What happened to Tateno-sensei?

03:18.932 --> 03:20.331
Gesomi?

03:20.433 --> 03:23.266
Tateno-sensei is
absent due to an injury.

03:23.369 --> 03:26.167
Is there a problem
with me being in charge?

03:26.272 --> 03:27.569
This is bad.

03:27.674 --> 03:31.303
If it was that old fart Tateno,
we could've cheated easily...

03:31.744 --> 03:34.304
Hey, what is Gesomi-sensei like?

03:34.781 --> 03:38.649
That's right. You just transferred
here, so you don't know.

03:38.751 --> 03:42.448
She devotes her life
to finding cheaters.

03:42.589 --> 03:46.685
She expelled many in the past.
I'd say she's extremely sadistic!

03:47.193 --> 03:49.821
Don't even think about cheating.

03:50.296 --> 03:53.493
Devoting her life
to such a stupid thing...

03:53.600 --> 03:54.897
Now, begin.

04:05.311 --> 04:06.300
Anego.

04:07.580 --> 04:08.979
What should we do?

04:09.082 --> 04:11.812
At this rate, we'll all repeat the grade.

04:11.918 --> 04:12.819
Anego...

04:12.819 --> 04:14.218
Anego...
I know!

04:14.320 --> 04:17.084
Don't take your eyes off
Gesomi no matter what.

04:17.190 --> 04:20.216
We can catch her off guard,
even for an instant.

04:20.326 --> 04:21.657
Right.

04:26.299 --> 04:27.596
Now!

04:42.915 --> 04:44.644
Such an old trick...

04:45.885 --> 04:48.115
Isn't there anyone out there?

04:48.955 --> 04:53.551
Cheaters with unique methods
to present a serious challenge.

05:00.867 --> 05:03.392
Get up, you rotten oranges.

05:04.771 --> 05:07.137
I'll give you another chance.

05:07.240 --> 05:12.109
Next time, try to cheat in
a way that will actually excite me.

05:12.812 --> 05:14.074
That is...

05:15.181 --> 05:18.514
...if you have a brain
inside that head of yours.

05:19.319 --> 05:21.310
We're not oranges!

05:22.422 --> 05:23.323
We're human beings!

05:23.323 --> 05:25.291
We're human beings!
That's right!

05:26.993 --> 05:30.986
Oh my. You're rotten, but you
can still say nasty things.

05:31.497 --> 05:32.964
What'd you say?

05:33.066 --> 05:37.059
Jeez, Anego-san
gets excited very easily.

05:37.170 --> 05:38.432
What'd you say?

05:38.538 --> 05:41.200
Now's my chance. Come on out.

05:45.211 --> 05:46.576
Understood.

05:46.679 --> 05:48.670
Worry not, Punie-dono.

05:48.781 --> 05:53.377
We studied all night and
mastered the essence of academics.

05:57.190 --> 05:59.818
Those are the veggies from the curry!

05:59.926 --> 06:03.919
Punie-chan's going to let those
manservants do all the cheating.

06:09.035 --> 06:11.731
This is math, Punie-dono?

06:11.838 --> 06:13.897
Right. Hurry up.

06:19.212 --> 06:22.511
Punie-dono, are you aware of this?

06:22.582 --> 06:23.416
What?

06:23.416 --> 06:27.250
We're vegetables given
life by the power of magic.

06:27.353 --> 06:29.082
Temporary puppets.

06:29.422 --> 06:34.826
And so our skills can't be greater
than the one who gave us life.

06:35.561 --> 06:37.995
You can't go beyond my skills?

06:38.798 --> 06:40.197
N-No...

06:40.333 --> 06:44.133
That's right. I am loath
to say this, but this problem...

06:44.904 --> 06:46.838
...is gibberish to me.

06:47.173 --> 06:48.140
What?

06:48.941 --> 06:50.465
I'm sorry.

06:50.777 --> 06:52.176
You're useless.

06:52.545 --> 06:55.878
S-Since it has turned to this,
I will commit hara-kiri!

06:55.982 --> 06:57.415
Potato-dono!

06:57.517 --> 07:00.452
I will atone for my sin by killing myself!

07:00.553 --> 07:02.885
This is for Punie-dono!

07:02.989 --> 07:04.149
Hold it!

07:04.257 --> 07:05.519
Let go!

07:05.625 --> 07:09.652
No, I won't! Death isn't
the only thing for vegetables!

07:09.762 --> 07:12.663
I'm begging you! For pity's sake!

07:13.399 --> 07:14.491
Shut up.

07:14.600 --> 07:19.094
If your suicide could keep me from
being left back, then I needn't suffer.

07:19.806 --> 07:21.364
Is something wrong?

07:21.974 --> 07:23.305
It's nothing.

07:25.378 --> 07:28.643
You people, come
to the detention room later.

07:30.650 --> 07:32.777
Why you... Just wait.

07:37.390 --> 07:39.290
I'm exhausted...

07:56.909 --> 07:59.742
To my loyal vegetables...

08:00.379 --> 08:05.544
This deep situation with the exam,
after looking at my current state...

08:05.651 --> 08:11.146
We must resort to an emergency
measure and keep control of events.

08:12.058 --> 08:13.855
Punie-sama...

08:15.361 --> 08:18.853
The time is 10:20, and this
plan will come to an end.

08:18.965 --> 08:23.265
It's very unfortunate, but we're
going to give up on this exam.

08:23.369 --> 08:26.497
You can return
to being normal vegetables.

08:26.839 --> 08:28.966
Then you'll repeat the grade?

08:29.509 --> 08:30.976
I will not.

08:32.912 --> 08:37.246
Lyrical Tokarev, kill them all!

08:45.458 --> 08:50.395
I can't let them find out the princess
from the land of magic is stupid.

08:50.930 --> 08:54.593
If they were to find out...
If they were to find out...

08:56.802 --> 09:00.602
I'm going to blow up this planet
and take everyone with me!

09:06.379 --> 09:08.506
That's a Magical A-weapon!

09:08.614 --> 09:11.174
Don't, Punie! If you let that explode...

09:11.284 --> 09:15.880
...it'll turn everything in a radius
of one hundred to smithereens!

09:19.392 --> 09:23.658
You're willing to choose
death over failing an exam?

09:32.004 --> 09:34.871
I haven't teamed up
with you since Vietnam.

09:34.974 --> 09:39.411
Hurry, paya! It's possible
Punie-chan will jump the gun, paya!

09:40.179 --> 09:42.477
Don't worry. No problem.

09:42.582 --> 09:44.880
Leave it to Peter.

09:50.623 --> 09:52.284
That school, right?

09:58.898 --> 10:00.024
George!

10:03.169 --> 10:07.663
Bill! Ronald! Jimmy! Richard!

10:07.773 --> 10:10.503
Abraham!

10:11.978 --> 10:13.707
What? What's going on?

10:17.216 --> 10:19.878
You okay? You're not that hurt!

10:21.253 --> 10:22.948
Hang in there!

10:23.689 --> 10:27.887
Why is it so dark?
Is this the new Tanna Tunnel?

10:28.995 --> 10:32.453
The prototype is passing
Gifu-Hashima Station.

10:32.999 --> 10:34.033
Where do I get off?

10:34.033 --> 10:35.933
Where do I get off?
Medic! Medic!

10:40.373 --> 10:43.467
This looks bad.
Let's try to get her out of here.

10:43.576 --> 10:44.634
R-Right.

10:45.077 --> 10:50.140
There's a bullet train stationed every
30 minutes at Annakaharuna Station...

10:50.249 --> 10:53.047
Hang on! That's just a delusion!

10:56.555 --> 10:57.579
Hey!

11:00.726 --> 11:12.695
<i>Climb Nitakayama 1208</i>

11:19.011 --> 11:20.137
Tetsuko Koku

11:24.116 --> 11:26.084
<i>Punie Tanaka</i>

11:29.522 --> 11:38.021
<i>Tora! Tora! Tora!</i>

11:38.464 --> 11:40.728
Good job, paya! Let's flee, paya!

11:41.100 --> 11:42.624
Aye aye, sir!

11:43.269 --> 11:47.968
That was close, paya.
It was about to turn ugly, paya.

11:48.074 --> 11:49.405
Payatan.

11:50.109 --> 11:51.770
What is it, paya?

11:52.545 --> 11:56.845
Can you come back to
the squad, Colonel Paya Livingston?

11:57.283 --> 11:58.375
Squad?

12:00.086 --> 12:01.849
The squad, huh?

12:19.105 --> 12:21.130
Let's not talk about that.

12:21.240 --> 12:24.334
I'm just a magical girl's mascot now.

12:25.311 --> 12:26.608
Colonel...

12:29.248 --> 12:30.943
Sorry about that!

12:31.917 --> 12:33.908
Forget it!

12:34.386 --> 12:37.014
Okay, paya! I'll forget, paya!

12:41.861 --> 12:43.453
What was that?

12:44.296 --> 12:47.265
Don't tell me someone
used the army to cheat...

12:48.868 --> 12:50.028
Oh my.

12:51.337 --> 12:54.670
That's it, folks!
Pass up your papers from the back.

12:55.007 --> 12:56.975
Who could take a test this way!

12:57.076 --> 12:58.976
Something's wrong with you, Gesomi!

12:59.078 --> 13:00.636
Yeah! Yeah!

13:04.817 --> 13:06.216
That's too bad...

13:06.318 --> 13:09.481
Even though you're stupid,
I'll still be your friend.

13:10.089 --> 13:12.216
It was Punie, all right.

13:12.858 --> 13:14.348
She got a zero...

13:14.460 --> 13:17.952
...but she didn't get left back
due to good overall marks.

13:18.063 --> 13:20.088
Happy ending indeed.

13:28.908 --> 13:30.739
Good morning, Anego-san.

13:32.945 --> 13:35.004
We've met every morning lately.

13:35.114 --> 13:37.241
Y-Yeah, that's true.

13:38.117 --> 13:41.052
We'll be late if we don't hurry. Later.

13:41.754 --> 13:43.654
Hey, Yamada...

13:49.728 --> 13:53.425
What the hell.
I can't believe a person like me...

13:54.133 --> 13:56.124
...would fall in love.

13:59.004 --> 14:01.734
But falling in love isn't my thing.

14:04.009 --> 14:07.103
If they found out,
I wonder what everyone would say.

14:07.213 --> 14:10.376
I have to make sure
no one finds out...

14:12.384 --> 14:14.215
I found a great toy.

14:14.320 --> 14:15.354
Paya.

14:15.354 --> 14:18.619
<i>Episode 6: When I Saw You Sweep
Back Your Bangs Under the Apple Tree</i>

14:18.724 --> 14:22.057
<i>with the Flower-comb in Your Hair,
I Thought You Were a Flower Too...</i>

14:26.398 --> 14:28.389
Hey, confessed to Yamada yet?

14:29.702 --> 14:30.862
Come here!

14:32.671 --> 14:35.231
You didn't tell anyone, did you?

14:35.341 --> 14:36.831
Of course not.

14:36.942 --> 14:41.743
You have strong feelings for him.
Why would I go tell others about it?

14:42.181 --> 14:43.580
Do you know?

14:43.682 --> 14:44.450
What?

14:44.450 --> 14:46.941
What?
About Anego-san and Yamada-kun...

14:50.289 --> 14:52.086
Can't help that it's out.

14:52.191 --> 14:54.955
That's right. I'm in love.

14:55.361 --> 14:56.794
That's wonderful!

14:56.896 --> 14:59.865
But it won't work.
I've already given up.

14:59.965 --> 15:01.125
Why?

15:01.834 --> 15:04.826
I'm the leader
who's in control of this area.

15:04.937 --> 15:08.634
But compared to me,
he was brought up sheltered.

15:08.741 --> 15:12.233
He has a good personality,
and everyone loves him.

15:12.344 --> 15:15.472
We're like night and day. It won't work.

15:15.581 --> 15:21.486
Oh, but those are the types of
people that tend to be insidious.

15:21.587 --> 15:25.045
A brute and a hussy.
You'll make a great couple.

15:25.157 --> 15:27.352
Don't base things on your values!

15:27.459 --> 15:30.917
Anyway, I decided not to get
too deep. Leave me alone.

15:31.030 --> 15:32.622
That's really okay?

15:32.731 --> 15:33.959
You're annoying.

15:34.066 --> 15:38.503
Feeling nervous when confessing...
Feeling excited waiting for the reply...

15:38.604 --> 15:42.062
But when they turn you down,
you become very sad.

15:42.174 --> 15:46.702
I think those are special
privileges that only girls have.

15:46.812 --> 15:47.836
Punie...

15:47.947 --> 15:49.676
Here, take this.

15:50.015 --> 15:53.678
I'm sorry about before.
Punie-chan is right.

15:53.786 --> 15:57.745
You can have this. I won this from
Monthly Railroad Fan magazine.

15:57.856 --> 15:59.721
Amusement park tickets!

15:59.825 --> 16:03.625
That's right.
You should ask if he wants to go.

16:03.729 --> 16:04.923
Well, but...

16:05.264 --> 16:06.526
Come on!

16:09.268 --> 16:10.462
Go! Go!

16:22.881 --> 16:25.042
Hey, Anego-san. What is it?

16:25.150 --> 16:26.674
Oh, well...

16:27.419 --> 16:31.287
Um, do you have
any plans this weekend?

16:31.757 --> 16:34.419
No, I'm free. Why?

16:34.526 --> 16:36.585
I understand if you don't want to...

16:36.695 --> 16:40.222
...but I got these tickets
for an amusement park.

16:40.332 --> 16:42.527
Would you like to go with me?

16:42.634 --> 16:43.726
Sure.

16:43.836 --> 16:44.860
Really?

16:44.970 --> 16:47.803
I've been wanting
to go there for a while.

16:51.744 --> 16:53.678
My good friends!

16:53.979 --> 16:56.447
You did it, Anego-san!

16:56.548 --> 16:59.813
I'm sorry about
before, Punie, Tetsuko.

16:59.918 --> 17:01.749
Have a great time.

17:17.036 --> 17:18.628
He's running late.

17:18.771 --> 17:20.204
Yeah.

17:21.607 --> 17:23.370
I can hear Punie's voice!

17:23.475 --> 17:25.875
Huh? Something's in my ear.

17:25.978 --> 17:28.742
We'll advise you
from behind the scenes.

17:28.847 --> 17:30.315
Good luck, Anego-san!

17:30.315 --> 17:32.146
Good luck, Anego-san!
I don't need your help!

17:32.251 --> 17:36.244
Oh? Who do you think
made this date possible?

17:36.655 --> 17:38.418
Hey, here he comes.

17:38.524 --> 17:40.014
Left! Left!

17:40.959 --> 17:42.859
Sorry about that!

17:45.397 --> 17:47.160
Sorry I'm late. Wait long?

17:47.266 --> 17:49.291
No, not at all.

17:49.401 --> 17:50.969
She said she didn't wait.

17:50.969 --> 17:54.029
She said she didn't wait.
She came an hour early too.

17:54.540 --> 17:57.276
I'll kill them...
I'll kill them later for sure...

17:57.276 --> 17:59.540
Mouse Land

18:02.781 --> 18:04.908
What should we ride first?

18:05.017 --> 18:06.382
Let's see...

18:06.485 --> 18:08.646
How about the roller coaster?

18:08.720 --> 18:09.687
Good idea.

18:09.788 --> 18:14.020
Go and tell him. Say you
want to ride the roller coaster.

18:14.126 --> 18:15.252
Come on!

18:15.360 --> 18:17.885
I have no say in this?

18:21.066 --> 18:26.163
If they enjoy plenty of thrills, their bond
will become stronger than ever.

18:26.271 --> 18:27.135
Really?

18:31.143 --> 18:34.704
But somehow,
this doesn't look thrilling at all...

18:35.147 --> 18:36.341
I know!

18:37.549 --> 18:41.747
Lyrical Tokarev, kill them all!

18:42.287 --> 18:46.246
Spirits, provide
more thrills for Anego-san!

18:46.925 --> 18:49.621
I'm really scared of things like this.

18:49.728 --> 18:53.255
I'm perfectly fine.
I'm not scared at all...

19:02.774 --> 19:05.038
This kind of feels too high...

19:24.897 --> 19:28.663
I was a fool.
I should've never listened to her.

19:28.767 --> 19:31.361
This is a strange amusement park.

19:31.470 --> 19:33.938
Hey, should we go there now?

19:34.673 --> 19:36.436
We're going already?

19:36.542 --> 19:40.000
I'm begging you, Punie.
Leave us alone...

19:40.112 --> 19:43.047
What are you saying?
The real fun begins here.

19:43.148 --> 19:47.052
You're on an amusement-park
date, so you have to go there.

19:47.052 --> 19:51.512
<i>Mansion of Fear</i>

19:52.057 --> 19:55.515
Wow, a mansion of fear.
Sounds good.

19:55.961 --> 20:01.228
Holding each other out of fear
of the dark... And while they're at it...

20:01.333 --> 20:04.564
What are you trying
to make me say, Punie-chan?

20:04.670 --> 20:06.763
Oh, stop it!

20:08.874 --> 20:14.107
I prepared the greatest terror of all.
I'll make you regret ever being born.

20:14.213 --> 20:17.011
If it's man-made, it's not scary at all...

20:17.115 --> 20:20.448
...but if it's Punie,
who knows what could happen?

20:20.552 --> 20:23.020
This is bad. I want to go home...

20:26.325 --> 20:27.426
Are you trembling?

20:27.426 --> 20:29.189
Are you trembling?
N-No way!

20:29.294 --> 20:32.229
Don't worry. I'm here by your side.

20:32.331 --> 20:33.593
Let's go!

20:33.999 --> 20:37.093
I-I-I'm holding hands with him!

20:37.903 --> 20:39.803
Thank you, Punie!

20:47.646 --> 20:50.843
It's so dark that I can't see anything.

21:08.100 --> 21:10.227
I'm kind of nervous.

21:21.980 --> 21:23.379
The highway?

21:23.482 --> 21:26.610
Anego-san, how do
you like the mansion of fear?

21:26.718 --> 21:28.345
I don't know...

21:30.389 --> 21:33.916
The bloodcurdling
terror I prepared for you...

21:34.493 --> 21:38.827
It's a drive on the metropolitan
highway, and the driver is...

21:40.465 --> 21:44.663
...a car-manga-influenced, newly
licensed idiot who thinks he can drive!

21:47.472 --> 21:49.997
Don't worry! Really!
I'm really dangerous!

21:50.108 --> 21:53.043
I'm really good at driving!
I'm really dangerous!

21:53.145 --> 21:55.136
Idiot! Eyes on the road!

21:55.247 --> 21:58.478
They are!
I'll never get into an accident!

21:58.583 --> 22:00.175
You're annoying!

22:00.485 --> 22:02.953
Yeah! This is such a great feeling!

22:03.055 --> 22:04.955
I'll do the counter!

22:12.831 --> 22:16.767
Wow, I'm drifting! This can't be real!

22:16.868 --> 22:18.733
You're spinning, idiot!

22:18.837 --> 22:23.467
I'm not an idiot! I'm really smart!
I can get into Tokyo University!

22:29.281 --> 22:32.250
<i>Punie Tanaka's Store
(For Personal Use)</i>

22:35.721 --> 22:37.552
<i>Great Magic Ridge</i>

22:38.857 --> 22:41.417
This is great! It's really great!

22:41.526 --> 22:45.189
This is better than mugging people!
Should I drift again?

22:45.964 --> 22:47.056
Okay!

22:47.165 --> 22:50.191
This is great!
I'm a genius! A super genius!

22:52.604 --> 22:54.071
Where do I shift up?

22:54.172 --> 22:59.007
No, that's reverse. I'm not even
stepping on the clutch. This is a hoot.

23:37.416 --> 23:39.884
Are you okay, Yamada-kun?

23:41.052 --> 23:44.488
I don't want to go on
dates anymore! Mama!

23:58.103 --> 23:59.468
It's over.

24:01.072 --> 24:02.869
My first love...

24:08.413 --> 24:12.349
And what happened to
Anego-san afterwards...

24:26.431 --> 24:28.365
What are you looking at?

24:36.641 --> 24:39.474
She's gotten
even worse than before...

24:40.212 --> 24:41.746
You'll be unattractive.

24:41.746 --> 24:43.907
You'll be unattractive.
Shut up!

25:02.601 --> 25:10.440
<i>If you bend the knees upside down...</i>

25:10.709 --> 25:18.047
<i>...even your belief about
crushing a rock becomes distorted.</i>

25:18.717 --> 25:26.214
<i>Good, justice, and even the truth
is gone when you feel the pain.</i>

25:26.324 --> 25:34.732
<i>Even those with fortitude have joints.</i>

25:34.866 --> 25:42.739
<i>Take a look. This is
the submission of a monarch.</i>

25:42.941 --> 25:55.081
<i>As long as you
have fortitude, you will prosper.</i>

26:17.442 --> 26:22.607
Next, "Don't Think Participation
Is Important. That's Too Lenient."

26:22.714 --> 26:25.205
"We Can't Just
Stay the Way We Are."

26:25.317 --> 26:27.945
"It's Kind of Scary
Becoming an Adult."

26:28.053 --> 26:29.611
Choo-choo!
